==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|ende||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ent-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ende}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ende}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*andī}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*andijaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂entíos}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ent-||front, forehead}}.

See also {{cog|nl|einde}}, {{cog|de|Ende}}, {{cog|no|ende}}, {{cog|sv|ände}}; also {{cog|sga|ét||end, point}}, {{cog|la|antiae||forelock}}, {{cog|sq|anë||side}}, {{cog|grc|ἀντίος||opposite}}, {{cog|sa|अन्त्य||last}}.  More at {{m|en|and}} and {{m|en|anti-}}.

The verb is from {{der|en|enm|enden}}, {{m|enm|endien}}, from {{der|en|ang|endian||to end, to make an end of, complete, finish, abolish, destroy, come to an end, die}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*andijōną||to finish, end}}, denominative from {{m|gem-pro|*andijaz}}.

